  "query_preview": "..\nMoisture associated with the northern edge of Invest 99W continues to\nimpact Guam and Rota with trade wind showers with Tinian and Saipan \nstaying dryer today. While there are currently no thunderstorms in\nthe vicinity, increasing wind shear, sufficient moisture, and a\ndeveloping 99W will allow for isolated thunderstorms tonight through\nmuch of this week for the whole Marianas. Models are in agreement for\n99W to develop near Yap and move into the Phillipine Sea. Therefore,\nthe main threat to the Marianas will be the potential for locally \nheavy rainfall as remnants of Invest 90W merge with outer bands of\n99W that could be enhanced by the strong ongoing westerly wind \nburst. Rainfall totals will depend on the speed, strength, and track\nof 99W. This situation remains uncertain and will be monitored \nclosely. However, the potential for a tropical disturbance to impact\nthe region next week is very low.",
